  "id": "transient-monocular-blindness",
  "term": "transient monocular blindness",
  "definition": "Transient monocular blindness is a sudden, painless, temporary loss of vision in one eye. It is most commonly linked to carotid atherothromboembolism, although some cases may involve impaired venous outflow and resulting ocular venous hypertension.",
